  "header": {
    "subsystemType": "Hrot.Scenario",
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "demo-city",
    "description": "What: on demo-city a physical 'Blue Company' (CompanyAttack at 10 s: Objective 1 (425,425), then Objective 2 (645,445)) with THREE platoons: one STOCHASTIC (30 men from the TKB composite, no bodies; first on the roster, so the company gives it the assault) and two PHYSICAL (two squads of four men each: a base of fire and a reserve). No enemy: the routing is what is tested. Judge: every order reaches the right KIND of unit - the stochastic platoon runs the generic StochasticUnitAttack, the physical ones their physical plays (PlatoonSupportByFire, PlatoonDefend), never the other way round - and the attack completes: the stochastic platoon reaches Objective 1, and the HoldArea objective there (80 m, 25 men - only the stochastic platoon's 30 slot-table men can meet it) reads Achieved. Fail: a platoon given the wrong kind of play, or the objective never held. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh agg-mixed-company-attack"
  },
